				"227161A851D43479"
			]
			description: [
				"Wood spirit distils at &eWarm&r into acetone and methanol, leaving vinegar. Acetone and methanol boil only 9 °C apart, so a bare still brings them over slowly; column pieces fix that."
				""
				"Vinegar strips copper's patina the way acid strips rust."
			]
