			description: [
				"Carbolic oil settles in a settling flask into naphthalene and strained carbolic oil. Shaken with caustic soda in a separating funnel, the strained oil gives sodium phenolate under a layer of creosote."
				""
				"Sodium phenolate stirred with carbon dioxide in a vat gives phenol and soda ash. Carbon dioxide comes off fermenting and burning lime, by pipe only: it has no bucket."
